  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<p>Type of paradise fish. IUCN Red List: LC.</p><p>The Black paradise fish is a dark-colored, gourami-like fish with a beautiful black outline on the scales. Unlike bettas, these fish tolerate their peers and usually establish a pecking order in groups. They are very hardy and tolerant of different water temperatures, making them great beginner fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<p>Native to central Vietnam, particularly the Thu Bồn River system in Quảng Nam province and the Hương (Perfume) River basin in Thừa Thiên-Huế province.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<p>A pair can be kept together in a 10 to 20-gallon tank (about 40–75 litres).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: ~60+ (can tolerate high TDS water)</li><li>pH: 6.0–7.8 (water quality isn't that important)</li><li>Temperature: 21–28 °C (70–83 °F); does well in cooler temperatures, but higher temperatures induce coloration and breeding behaviour</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Readily take dried foods. Fed on blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<p>Somewhat territorial, but can be kept in groups as long as there is enough space. A pair per 5 gallons (about 19 litres) of water is recommended.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<p>Males have extended anal, dorsal and caudal fins, while females have a much rounder body.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<p>Bubble nester.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/black-paradise-fish-macropodus-spechti",
      "html": "<p>Maximum size: about 13 cm (5 inches) including tail.</p>"
    }
  ],
